[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-50202"] :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨{e}^{t}-4,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$, then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨{e}^{t}-4,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t}-4,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int ({e}^{t}-4)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}-4t+{c}_{1},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}-4t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}-4t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-99264/selection/2f0f3e06a7bd2702d65f2a11394d871b87d08170e77e54b00bfc23c22d0e23da" :answer/id #uuid "26a71e89-29b4-5bc7-9b10-b54090db6210" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{t}^{5},\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99264/selection/0c2863ade767dd8cd5774ead2c06f87e673fa6ae5120a7e31c9f72d45f739c6b" :answer/id #uuid "f0253e6b-be11-5dc1-99d5-7426ec4d4c83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{t}^{5},\\,-\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99264/selection/7c9016c95609828386910a76f25061432b547fd5fa7d6724f5b695c2f7421c81" :answer/id #uuid "c6110327-632b-5e5f-bf7a-0617a23a71b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99264/selection/e9657b255d20bab208268d9a71e1da25217d6e7ef5942eca55333884ad39f7a1" :answer/id #uuid "654378c7-1b93-5365-9376-0fbd0c1eddff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99264/selection/18205ae6d5bbde78efdd723433302fecee494dd95db66d35e8ac01b702dbef22" :answer/id #uuid "7c94ed39-4373-551c-b06c-a1face0ceeb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4},\\,\\frac{3}{{t}^{3}}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99264/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b59ed963-fef5-5a46-8d25-f85418d99e14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-99264/selection/2f0f3e06a7bd2702d65f2a11394d871b87d08170e77e54b00bfc23c22d0e23da" :answer-field/choices ["q-99264/selection/2f0f3e06a7bd2702d65f2a11394d871b87d08170e77e54b00bfc23c22d0e23da" "q-99264/selection/0c2863ade767dd8cd5774ead2c06f87e673fa6ae5120a7e31c9f72d45f739c6b" "q-99264/selection/7c9016c95609828386910a76f25061432b547fd5fa7d6724f5b695c2f7421c81" "q-99264/selection/e9657b255d20bab208268d9a71e1da25217d6e7ef5942eca55333884ad39f7a1" "q-99264/selection/18205ae6d5bbde78efdd723433302fecee494dd95db66d35e8ac01b702dbef22"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-99264" :question/id #uuid "978f19ce-bf8b-567e-979e-75fe1636e0f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-99264" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨5{t}^{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\text{ }5{t}^{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨5{t}^{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 5{t}^{4}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{5}+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{1}{t}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{5},\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{5},\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-99264/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99264"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-80460"] :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t}⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\,{e}^{t}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\,{e}^{t}⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-123224/selection/415c89f30ae15d780b81b45c641cec152fdc4c6b54020badb2bb6cd3c8e7124b" :answer/id #uuid "9718da6a-a6d4-578f-a9c3-2f206c80893d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123224/selection/d8e5cf6c29a8af0edb59d6ee8a54ca30fd668e934b5a630966723f6a66f3d01b" :answer/id #uuid "9a6de13a-1cff-5322-a826-c0d7072def1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123224/selection/f3ae0d52177f6f60cf3a51adf0fa10b5ac4aff5ac24b07c20107785bac49f044" :answer/id #uuid "abddcc28-4e8f-52e1-97ec-9cbdf72a424f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123224/selection/fd059ddb9a0d99ec26d09b072e7b92e8fe7d0c1633e844ae6f6165af64aebb0d" :answer/id #uuid "82637355-748d-5358-ab04-687b5c68f99b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123224/selection/80b042a95811ebfe61f6cc1df5de6d6bc9cbdc1d8695f0e62